  "body": "# fix(examples): refresh the guide-multiaxis cached toolpath to the #3080 behaviour\n\n## What changed\n\n`examples/guide-multiaxis.camproj` kept a cached `FirstTraverseLow`\nwarning for `Indexed Face1` in the pre-#3080 form: the heights in the\nlocal frame of the tilted plane (`height_mm: 10.0`, `top_mm: 11.114`,\n`tilted: false`).\n\nThe file was regenerated through its own headless path: a\n`camcraft-cli script` run with `open_project`, `generate` of\n`Indexed Face1` only, and `save_project`. The cache now holds the\nwarning in the user's frame: `height_mm: 30.0`, `top_mm: 31.114`,\n`tilted: true`. The raise is the same 1.114 mm. The diff is five lines:\nthe four warning fields and the project `version` step-up of the save.\n`Swarf1` and every move are untouched; the file has no `.nc` output.\n\n## How verified\n\n- `guide_projects::indexed_guide_preserves_legacy_basis_and_path` - ok\n- `guide_projects::demo_projects_build_and_load_with_valid_paths` (the\n  reload-notes check over all three guide projects) - ok\n- `guide_projects::a_legacy_first_traverse_warning_matches_only_the_same_raise` - ok\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: nothing in `crates/`\n  changed, so the quick gate has no test steps for this diff.\n- `cargo xtask catalog --check`: red on `2d/drill-overfeed` (missing\n  `drill-overfeed.nc`). This is pre-existing on `origin/main` and not\n  touched by this PR: the case is `expect = \"refusal\"` with a committed\n  `refusal.txt`, and the checker still demands the `.nc` file.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The guide's pixel images (`cargo xtask docs-images`) were not built;\n  the toolpath moves did not change, so the rendered geometry is the\n  same.\n- The site test suite (`site/tests/test_guide_images.py`) was not run;\n  it reads the project JSON, whose only semantic change is the warning\n  form the guide already documents in both frames.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #3234\n",
